1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,520
Hello and welcome to this massive open online course, Introduction to BiRisk Management.

2
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:10,620
In this short video which will accompany your lecture slides, I will be discussing

3
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:18,400
the engineering control with specific reference to the facility design and the instrumentation

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,060
associated with this particular facility.

5
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:30,560
I am now at this mechanical control floor and this is a floor which is responsible for

6
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:37,560
controlling all the heating, ventilation and air conditioning equipment in this facility.

7
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,060
We will start off with this panel which is controlled from a computer below and this

8
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:51,400
panel controls all the motors and the compressors at this facility.

9
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:55,640
This over here in blue is the air handling unit.

10
00:00:55,640 --> 00:01:01,760
The air handling unit comprises a HEPA filter which filters all the air that enters this

11
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:11,040
facility and as you can see these filters can be opened for periodic maintenance and

12
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:15,840
for replacement of the filter modules.

13
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:22,680
So all the air entering this facility is filtered through this HEPA filter and the air which

14
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:30,160
exits this facility is filtered through these HEPA filters as well.

15
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:34,620
Now there are compressors here and these compressors are responsible for maintaining

16
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:41,940
the pressure of the water and the air which is supplied to this facility.

17
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:50,680
Each of the rooms over the units which are located in the floor below is connected to

18
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:55,510
its own individual HEPA filter.

19
00:01:55,510 --> 00:02:03,550
Now if you look at this instrument, this is actually a damper which regulates the flow

20
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:09,470
of air within the facility by opening and closing a valve known as a damper.

21
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:17,210
I will be discussing the dampers in the lecture notes.

22
00:02:17,210 --> 00:02:26,490
This is another larger HEPA filter unit which is basically an exhaust unit and it will filter

23
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:34,350
out all the particulates from the air exiting this facility before it is released out into

24
00:02:34,350 --> 00:02:36,190
the environment.

25
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:46,110
I will proceed now into the outer space to show you the stroboscopic fans.

26
00:02:46,110 --> 00:02:52,550
These are the high flume fans, what are known as strobic air fans.

27
00:02:52,610 --> 00:03:02,130
Now all the air which exits from this facility is passed through a HEPA filter and these fans

28
00:03:02,130 --> 00:03:09,490
will have a high pressure flume of air which is directed high into the environment.

29
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:16,450
This ensures that all the pathogens are effectively filtered out from this facility prior to release

30
00:03:16,450 --> 00:03:20,020
into the environment.

31
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:27,260
I will be discussing all these instrumentation in my lecture notes on facility design as part

32
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:29,260
of this MOOC.

33
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:31,260
Thank you.
